From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 22:13:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 42/79] fix(github-pr-review): let the member scan see control
 beads (gcp-m7dn)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Self-review catch, found by probing the live store rather than the fixtures.

workflow_outcome.py's member cross-check ran a plain `gc bd list
--metadata-field gc.root_bead_id=...`, which hides infra, template and gate
beads by default. Those hidden classes are precisely where a graph.v2 workflow
records a failure — the check, scope-check and gate control beads — so the scan
was blind to the beads a fail-closed reader most needs. The primary signal (the
root's own gc.outcome) was unaffected, but the backstop was weaker than it read.

Pass --include-templates --include-infra --include-gates. On a workflow with no
control beads the flags are a no-op (verified: same 7 members with and without
them on gcp-yxau), so this only widens what the scan can see.

Live verification against the real store, which also confirms the whole premise
of this branch:

  root-outcome gcp-yxau  -> {"outcome":"pass",...}      exit 0
      a completed graph.v2 workflow root really does carry the engine-computed
      gc.outcome this gate reads.
  root-outcome gcp-9wz   -> {"outcome":"unknown",...}   exit 1
      a root that closed with NO gc.outcome reads as not-passed rather than
      passing by default.
  root-outcome gcp-m7dn  -> {"outcome":"incomplete",...} exit 1
      a still-open root is never mistaken for a terminated one.
---
 gascity/assets/scripts/workflow_outcome.py | 7 +++++++
 gascity/tests/test_workflow_outcome.py     | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gascity/assets/scripts/workflow_outcome.py b/gascity/assets/scripts/workflow_outcome.py
index a51002f..bdaf78d 100755
--- a/gascity/assets/scripts/workflow_outcome.py
+++ b/gascity/assets/scripts/workflow_outcome.py
@@ -137,6 +137,10 @@ def load_root(runner: Runner, root_bead_id: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
 
 
 def load_members(runner: Runner, root_bead_id: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
+    # The include-* flags matter: a workflow's failure is often recorded on a
+    # check/scope-check/gate control bead, and `gc bd list` hides those classes
+    # by default. Scanning without them would silently skip exactly the beads a
+    # fail-closed reader needs to see.
     beads = parse_bead_list(
         runner(
             [
@@ -147,6 +151,9 @@ def load_members(runner: Runner, root_bead_id: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
                 "--json",
                 "--limit",
                 "0",
+                "--include-templates",
+                "--include-infra",
+                "--include-gates",
                 "--metadata-field",
                 f"{ROOT_BEAD_ID_KEY}={root_bead_id}",
             ]
diff --git a/gascity/tests/test_workflow_outcome.py b/gascity/tests/test_workflow_outcome.py
index 65ee8cf..fbb65c7 100644
--- a/gascity/tests/test_workflow_outcome.py
+++ b/gascity/tests/test_workflow_outcome.py
@@ -170,6 +170,10 @@ class ResolveWorkflowOutcomeTest(unittest.TestCase):
         list_cmd = next(cmd for cmd in runner.calls if cmd[:3] == ["gc", "bd", "list"])
         self.assertIn("--all", list_cmd)
         self.assertIn(f"gc.root_bead_id={ROOT_ID}", list_cmd)
+        # Control beads (check, scope-check, gates) are where a workflow's
+        # failure gets recorded, and gc bd list hides them by default.
+        for flag in ("--include-templates", "--include-infra", "--include-gates"):
+            self.assertIn(flag, list_cmd)
 
 
 class ReviewGateTest(unittest.TestCase):
